<title>UK: UK gilt auction -- full results.</title>
<headline>UK gilt auction -- full results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue was announced by the Bank of England</p>
<p>ISSUER: H M Treasury</p>
<p>MATURITY: 2.0 BLN STG</p>
<p>COUPON: 7.0 PERCENT</p>
<p>MATURITY: 2002</p>
<p>AVERAGE ACCEPTED YIELD: 7.24 PCT</p>
<p>BID AMOUNT/COVER: 3.49</p>
<p>LOWEST ACCEPTED PRICE: 98.30</p>
<p>PCT ALLOCATED AT LOWEST PRICE: 19.5 PCT</p>
<p>NOTES: The highest accepted yield was 7.25 percent leaving a yield tail of one basis point. The price tail was 1/32.</p>
<p>Competitive bids worth 1,823.5 million stg were allotted. Non-competitive bids to GEMMS totalled 170 million stg while non-competitive bids to others amounted to 6.5 million.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
